{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"action\": \"advisory_preparation\",\n  \"summary\": \"End-to-end configuration loading requires a live Vault server; the normal dependency closure is otherwise sufficient. [Spring Cloud Vault Quick Start](https://docs.spring.io/spring-cloud-vault/reference/quickstart.html)\",\n  \"deterministic_setup\": [\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"docker_image\",\n      \"image\": \"hashicorp/vault:1.21.1\",\n      \"slug\": \"vault\",\n      \"reason\": \"Pinned official Vault image; this version is referenced by Spring Cloud Vault release tooling and supports the documented integration-test workflow. [Spring Cloud Vault releases](https://github.com/spring-cloud/spring-cloud-vault/releases)\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"agent_guidance\": \"Start an isolated ephemeral Vault server from the declared image, preferably dev mode over HTTP for baseline KV/config-data coverage. Dynamically map its port, wait for readiness, provision deterministic KV data, configure spring.application.name, spring.config.import=vault://, spring.cloud.vault.uri, spring.cloud.vault.scheme=http, spring.cloud.vault.authentication, and the test-only authentication value, then always stop and remove the server. Exercise default/contextual paths, profiles, optional imports, and fail-fast behavior. Use a test-local truststore if TLS-specific coverage is attempted.\",\n  \"risks\": [\n    \"The upstream quick start uses HTTPS and generated certificates; HTTP dev mode will not cover TLS behavior.\",\n    \"Tests require a working Docker daemon and reliable container cleanup.\"\n  ]\n}"}}
